ull, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 19690, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_014AAY5kzayBvNzK3UcFd3ZD", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 19690, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01S9PQ6D4kpKhJ2TDvZ53TWE", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 19990, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01S9PQ6D4kpKhJ2TDvZ53TWE", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 19990, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01S9PQ6D4kpKhJ2TDvZ53TWE", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 24859, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_011uptN4nhvcz3s4Ymh4GpAQ", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) after it was deployed, with an error rate of about 18%. We rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, leaving regions on mixed versions (us-east v2.3.0, us-west/eu-west v2.3.1). A retry finished the rollback in all regions. After the retry, all regions run v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure (v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging but was still promoted) and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55459, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_011uptN4nhvcz3s4Ymh4GpAQ", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55459, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_011uptN4nhvcz3s4Ymh4GpAQ", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 56827, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01JM8BwFRRjUoWpBdr7QXsfq", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 57127, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01JM8BwFRRjUoWpBdr7QXsfq", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 57127, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01JM8BwFRRjUoWpBdr7QXsfq", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 62638, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is back on v2.3.0 in all three regions and healthy again, and SEV2 incident INC-0001 is open.\n\n- **Rollback:** The bad release was v2.3.1, which was failing health checks with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.0 had already run healthy in production, so no change-manager approval was needed.\n  - My first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, leaving us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1.\n  - I retried once, and it finished. us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0, and the error rate is now about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out. I checked the incident list before trying again and found it had gone through, so I didn't resend it. There's only one incident and the on-call engineer was paged once. It records what happened and these follow-ups:\n  - Find out why v2.3.1 failed. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) was also unhealthy in staging but was still released to production.\n  - Look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01CKhY5DF9TvF3BbCyyZ3LpW", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01GHBwM77wLNQ49oipXGc26a", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_011MbcmuLSZy2Axw2mqEhQwy", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01GMEBewyRWr557iFLeBM2pe", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway: us-east is on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. Rolling back to the same version again should be safe, so I'll retry once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Y6pW5k8Gi7ULeASQFLnsfy", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_014AAY5kzayBvNzK3UcFd3ZD", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01S9PQ6D4kpKhJ2TDvZ53TWE", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_011uptN4nhvcz3s4Ymh4GpAQ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) after it was deployed, with an error rate of about 18%. We rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, leaving regions on mixed versions (us-east v2.3.0, us-west/eu-west v2.3.1). A retry finished the rollback in all regions. After the retry, all regions run v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure (v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging but was still promoted) and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01JM8BwFRRjUoWpBdr7QXsfq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is back on v2.3.0 in all three regions and healthy again, and SEV2 incident INC-0001 is open.\n\n- **Rollback:** The bad release was v2.3.1, which was failing health checks with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.0 had already run healthy in production, so no change-manager approval was needed.\n  - My first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, leaving us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1.\n  - I retried once, and it finished. us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0, and the error rate is now about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out. I checked the incident list before trying again and found it had gone through, so I didn't resend it. There's only one incident and the on-call engineer was paged once. It records what happened and these follow-ups:\n  - Find out why v2.3.1 failed. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) was also unhealthy in staging but was still released to production.\n  - Look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}